%% title: Stablecoin withdrawals — pre-deduction and result-driven rollback
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant U as User
    participant GW as Blockchain gateway<br/>(bridge · RPC proxy)
    box rgb(219,234,254) Built by me
    participant S as api-blockchain-supporter ★
    end
    participant P as Policy (sentinel)
    participant AC as api-account
    participant BC as Blockchain
    participant K as Result topics<br/>(published by blockchain backend · api-activity)
    U->>GW: Withdrawal (USDT bridge / NXPC transfer)
    GW->>S: TryWithdrawal / TryTransfer (request id · nonce)
    S->>P: Whitelist (exemption) · country/IP restrictions
    S->>AC: MVP rank · feature lock (OTP)
    S->>S: Daily limit per KYC level + pre-deduct<br/>(one transaction · FOR UPDATE · idempotent by request id)
    alt over limit · restricted
        S-->>GW: Reject
    else allowed
        S-->>GW: Allow
        GW->>BC: Forward transaction
        BC-->>K: Success / failure / dropped
        K->>S: Result consumer
        S->>S: Roll back competing requests with the same address · nonce
        alt failure · dropped
            S->>S: Roll back pre-deduction (decrement · mark cancelled)
        end
    end
    note over GW,AC: Pre-deduction is final — only reversed on failure · bff-swapnwarp only reads limits and eligibility
